<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chenqiao Mutiny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">960 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Chen Qiao Mutiny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chenqiao Mutiny was the coup of 960 CE in which troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-zhou">Later Zhou</a> commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Zhao Kuangyin</a> draped him in the imperial yellow robe and proclaimed him emperor. Zhao took the reign name Taizu. The event marked the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chenqiao-mutiny.jpg" alt="Chenqiao Mutiny" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Charles Seppings Wright · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhao_Kuangyin_is_proclaimed_emperor_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
